# The rocket blast's streaks frame by frame (real TF2; ours: streaks.scene):
# one rocket down 2fort's bridge into its floor about 150 units ahead,
# recorded every frame at 60 frames a second (`movie streaks`) for 30
# frames: the yellow streaks' (Explosion_Flashup, Explosion_CoreFlash:
# sprite trails) length per frame, for particles.md Open questions 7.
#   tools/tf2ref/tf2ref.py scene tools/tf2ref/scenes/streaks.tf2 --out <dir>
mp_disable_respawn_times 1
cl_drawhud 0
r_drawvgui 0
r_drawviewmodel 0
fov_desired 90
viewmodel_fov 54
fps_max 60
mat_colorcorrection 0
tf_weapon_criticals 0
host_framerate 0
bot_kick all
sleep 1
jointeam red
sleep 1
joinclass soldier
kill
sleep 7
use tf_weapon_rocketlauncher
setpos 0 -300 0
setang 25 90 0
sleep 3
shot streaks_idle
host_framerate 0.016667
movie streaks
wait 2
+attack
wait 2
-attack
wait 80
endmovie
host_framerate 0
